WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.440
Let's talk about Geralt's
relationship with Ciri.

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:04.560
It's really the beating heart
of the show.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.320
How has this bond changed Geralt
as a character?

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:10.000
I'm not too sure
if it's necessarily

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.280
changed Geralt
as a character.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:16.160
Geralt has an instinctual desire
to protect,

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.360
as we see in Season 1
when he's telling Roach

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:21.640
about the first monster
he killed.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:25.560
He's talking about protecting
someone against other people.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:26.640
Throughout his life,

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.960
he has then tried
to fight this instinct,

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.640
and, ultimately,
the instinct

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.120
ends up winning
a number of times,

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.160
and that ends up getting him
into more trouble.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.800
So this is actually more like
an unlocking for Geralt.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.560
She's the key to allow him
to really be

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.520
who he has always wanted to be.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.960
Freya, you had
an action-packed season.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:46.840
New family,
new Witcher powers,

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.960
not so many runs
through the woods.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.240
I don't know,
were you disappointed in that?

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.280
No, I was very relieved, yeah.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:56.840
It was long-awaited
to get to finally actually,

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.200
yeah, pick up a sword.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.880
Absolutely,
and you were wonderful.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.800
Anya, Yennefer had a lot of
difficult choices this season,

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.760
especially after the loss
of her magic,

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.840
which I personally
was very devastated about.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:08.320
-Yeah, me too.
-Yeah. How did you--

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.000
Imagine how Nilfgaard felt.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.640
Oh yeah.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:12.440
You should see the other guy.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:15.240
They were literally devastated.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.200
How did you feel
about the choices she made

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.840
with regard
to Geralt and Ciri?

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:21.920
Ooh.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:22.960
How do I feel about it?

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.360
I kind of went through
the motions, you know,

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:28.160
with Yennefer,
kind of moment to moment.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.920
In hindsight,
she made some rash decisions.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:35.480
But I think, you know,
she didn't know, you know,

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:37.880
how to deal with the brutality
of the world without magic,

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:41.760
so, you know, her decision
to sacrifice Ciri

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.520
was the right one
in the moment.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.080
And that's the thing
about this show,

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.520
is like there's no--
I don't know,

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:50.800
just it's up
to the audience

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:52.560
to kind of figure out
what's right or wrong.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.680
And it's the beauty of kind of
exposing so much of a character

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:59.400
is you get to see why
they make a certain decision.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.800
Joey, let's talk
all things Jaskier.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.440
We see him with his
fancy new alias this season,

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.000
the Sandpiper.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.000
If we include Dandelion
from the book,

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.640
so, what,
you have like three names now?

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:11.560
-Yeah.
-Well, what's that about?

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:17.320
Yeah, Lauren,
what's that about?

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:19.560
I think I'm gonna get
a new nickname per season.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.520
Oh yeah? Okay.
The Knife.

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:23.280
You're not allowed
to pick them.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.240
How is it exploring a new side
of your character this season?

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.760
He's way more emotionally
vulnerable this season.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:32.160
I think in Season 1,
I was doing--

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.600
we were working so closely
together,

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.080
and he had this, like,
boyishness,

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:38.360
like a joy in him,
this kind of light

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:39.880
to a lot of the darkness

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:41.040
that you were just
talking about, Henry.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.760
And he often felt like
it was his job

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:44.960
to brighten a room.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:48.800
And we get to see that desire
kind of really tested

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:51.000
in a world that is
incredibly dangerous.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.000
And for the first time
in his life,

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:56.520
he's getting the bejesus
kicked out of him

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:59.000
and he doesn't have his best
friend to come and help him.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.320
And he's willing
to put his life on the line

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:04.320
to--to, you know, finally do
something good with his life,

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.040
-do something morally good.
-Yeah.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.400
And that was... that was
the biggest treat for me.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.880
I got to see this textured,
detailed character

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:13.360
that Lauren was so keen
to bring to the show.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:14.600
Like what you see?

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.120
Be sure to check out
the full episode

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:17.360
of The Witcher: Unlocked,

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:19.800
the official Netflix Geeked
aftershow.

